(5673426, 822219, 31456, '<td valign="top">Did you know that in Romanian, "cascador" (literal English translation: "cascader") means "stuntman," although "cascada" (cascade) means waterfall? I guess the stuntmen of yore were waterfall leapers. Poor guys... <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=939305&amp;page=9#5673200" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">9</a></td>', 'Did you know that in Romanian, "cascador" (literal English translation: "cascader") means "stuntman," although "cascada" (cascade) means waterfall? I guess the stuntmen of yore were waterfall leapers. Poor guys... 9', '2009-10-03 18:54:48.000000', NULL, 1),
