(5674539, 824944, 102278, '<td valign="top">Wonderful character portrait. I love this style. 9</td>', 'Wonderful character portrait. I love this style. 9', '2009-10-04 16:55:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674546, 822234, 96881, '<td valign="top">Firstly, befire I get to the photo, is there a reason you chose to submit at 600px wide, instead of the maximum 720px........maybe it was to get under 200kb, but is is better, usually, to adjust the "quality" rather than shrinking the photo.........<br/>An interesting collection of rocks with some nice and subtle tones through them.  The refelections are good through this image, however the number of rocks, and the apttern they are in, does lead the eyes through the picture searching a little for a subject...........the rocks seem to make an s pattern through the image.............</td>', 'Firstly, befire I get to the photo, is there a reason you chose to submit at 600px wide, instead of the maximum 720px........maybe it was to get under 200kb, but is is better, usually, to adjust the "quality" rather than shrinking the photo.........An interesting collection of rocks with some nice and subtle tones through them.  The refelections are good through this image, however the number of rocks, and the apttern they are in, does lead the eyes through the picture searching a little for a subject...........the rocks seem to make an s pattern through the image.............', '2009-10-04 17:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674559, 822987, 96881, '<td valign="top">Tye composition of the image is very right leaning.  There is little on the left, and the main attention grabbing elements, the building, is in the far right of the image, partly cut off as well............To make the rocks and water more the subject, I think you needed a slightly more panoramic view, with some more space to the left of the image to move the building away from the line of third.  I presume the rocks are meant to be a feature of this image.  But in the black and white, this does not really work for me. I would have removed the lowest part of the rocks, and included some more sky, moving the horizon down to the 1/3 line, and with the space to the left included, would have made a stronger image for me.............</td>', 'Tye composition of the image is very right leaning.  There is little on the left, and the main attention grabbing elements, the building, is in the far right of the image, partly cut off as well............To make the rocks and water more the subject, I think you needed a slightly more panoramic view, with some more space to the left of the image to move the building away from the line of third.  I presume the rocks are meant to be a feature of this image.  But in the black and white, this does not really work for me. I would have removed the lowest part of the rocks, and included some more sky, moving the horizon down to the 1/3 line, and with the space to the left included, would have made a stronger image for me.............', '2009-10-04 17:07:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674564, 821712, 96881, '<td valign="top">Dont get the title, but that is just me.  Its a photography contest so in that sense, it does notmatter.<br/>A crisp, clean, great capture of the flower. The compositon of this is really very good, and I think something that took a little thought and arranging................It works really well.  <br/>Maybe the green in the leaves is a touch overdone, but the purple of the flower is brilliant and right.........just nudging the green sat down a touch might have removed the slight fake look on some areas of the leaves, but thats a minor thing.<br/>The border, honestly, its a bit of nothing.  Looks more to me like you wanted a little extra black space, so went with a purple 1pxline to be the least obtrusive.  I think a thinker line (2px) and them being a little closer to the flower, giving wider black bands, would have finished it off a little better..<br/>But, minor things.  A really good image...........</td>', 'Dont get the title, but that is just me.  Its a photography contest so in that sense, it does notmatter.A crisp, clean, great capture of the flower. The compositon of this is really very good, and I think something that took a little thought and arranging................It works really well.  Maybe the green in the leaves is a touch overdone, but the purple of the flower is brilliant and right.........just nudging the green sat down a touch might have removed the slight fake look on some areas of the leaves, but thats a minor thing.The border, honestly, its a bit of nothing.  Looks more to me like you wanted a little extra black space, so went with a purple 1pxline to be the least obtrusive.  I think a thinker line (2px) and them being a little closer to the flower, giving wider black bands, would have finished it off a little better..But, minor things.  A really good image...........', '2009-10-04 17:12:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674570, 820993, 96881, '<td valign="top">Maybe he is.  The image is really busy, with too many things trying to catch my eye.  The green light, the buildings, the moving car, and due to the title, the man.  Without the title, I would have almost missed him really...........even the sky is competing for the focus point............</td>', 'Maybe he is.  The image is really busy, with too many things trying to catch my eye.  The green light, the buildings, the moving car, and due to the title, the man.  Without the title, I would have almost missed him really...........even the sky is competing for the focus point............', '2009-10-04 17:17:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674575, 822517, 46918, '<td valign="top">LOL reminds me of Iraq.....This looks more like afghanistan though. Good job on the shot.</td>', 'LOL reminds me of Iraq.....This looks more like afghanistan though. Good job on the shot.', '2009-10-04 17:22:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674606, 820325, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: What a scene - certainly isn''t something I see every day! The lady''s pushing foot is priceless. Your focus is good, you''ve allowed yourself enough DOF to accommodate all of the area of interest.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I was a little puzzled - I had wondered why we weren''t looking at a slightly earlier time point - thinking the image may have been a little more compelling if we had seen this trio from the front; but I''ve now learnt that this is out of respect of the wishes of the subjects - great stuff.<br/> <br/>Overall: An image with bags of charm.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: What a scene - certainly isn''t something I see every day! The lady''s pushing foot is priceless. Your focus is good, you''ve allowed yourself enough DOF to accommodate all of the area of interest. Critical stuff: I was a little puzzled - I had wondered why we weren''t looking at a slightly earlier time point - thinking the image may have been a little more compelling if we had seen this trio from the front; but I''ve now learnt that this is out of respect of the wishes of the subjects - great stuff. Overall: An image with bags of charm.', '2009-10-04 18:13:09.000000', NULL, 1),
