(5674682, 824434, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: This is a very well executed and conceived image - an intriguing set up.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m about as anti-smoking as they come so I''m never going to be a fan of this image. Photographically it feels too close but perhaps it''s just me recoiling as I would in real life.<br/> <br/>Overall: An interesting vision, skilfully executed.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: This is a very well executed and conceived image - an intriguing set up. Critical stuff: I''m about as anti-smoking as they come so I''m never going to be a fan of this image. Photographically it feels too close but perhaps it''s just me recoiling as I would in real life. Overall: An interesting vision, skilfully executed.', '2009-10-04 19:30:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674683, 820636, 32011, '<td valign="top">This is by far my favourite image in this challenge... gave it an 8 on my first pass... bumped it to 9 on my second pass... and am now bumping it up to a 10 during my comment pass.  I absolutely love this photo... so, I''m going to fav it too.  Composition is perfect... as are all the other technical aspects of the image, but this also has a real WOW factor... truly inspiration work.  Well done.</td>', 'This is by far my favourite image in this challenge... gave it an 8 on my first pass... bumped it to 9 on my second pass... and am now bumping it up to a 10 during my comment pass.  I absolutely love this photo... so, I''m going to fav it too.  Composition is perfect... as are all the other technical aspects of the image, but this also has a real WOW factor... truly inspiration work.  Well done.', '2009-10-04 19:33:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674684, 824840, 32011, '<td valign="top">This is a fantastic photo... the tilt works here... adds a dynamic.  The grain, another element that often gets photos punished in voting, works wonders here.  Composition... LOVE it... wasn''t sure about the ball at first, and initially gave it an 8 (actually, I think this originally a 7 which I bumped to an 8... but now that I''m looking at it while commenting, I think it might warrant another nudge.  Nine it is.</td>', 'This is a fantastic photo... the tilt works here... adds a dynamic.  The grain, another element that often gets photos punished in voting, works wonders here.  Composition... LOVE it... wasn''t sure about the ball at first, and initially gave it an 8 (actually, I think this originally a 7 which I bumped to an 8... but now that I''m looking at it while commenting, I think it might warrant another nudge.  Nine it is.', '2009-10-04 19:33:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674685, 824985, 32011, '<td valign="top">I really, really like this... it''s different, but not in a bad way.  Composition is excellent, details are great, excellent use of shallow DOF.</td>', 'I really, really like this... it''s different, but not in a bad way.  Composition is excellent, details are great, excellent use of shallow DOF.', '2009-10-04 19:33:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674687, 825045, 32011, '<td valign="top">I love tilt-shift photos, be they real, or processed to look like it.  You''ve done exceptionally well with this image... colours, details, composition... all fantastic.  I''m curious to see how well the general DPC voters vote on this.  Hope it does well.</td>', 'I love tilt-shift photos, be they real, or processed to look like it.  You''ve done exceptionally well with this image... colours, details, composition... all fantastic.  I''m curious to see how well the general DPC voters vote on this.  Hope it does well.', '2009-10-04 19:34:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674689, 824703, 32011, '<td valign="top">As far as pet portraiture goes, you''ve absolutely nailed this!!!  This is a fantastic photo, processed perfectly, though, I wouldn''t be surprised if the DPC voting masses think it''s over done... thankfully, I''m not one of the masses and this is in the top 10 for the challenge in my books.  Well done, and I hope you get many more voters like me... would be nice to see this on the first page for the challenge.</td>', 'As far as pet portraiture goes, you''ve absolutely nailed this!!!  This is a fantastic photo, processed perfectly, though, I wouldn''t be surprised if the DPC voting masses think it''s over done... thankfully, I''m not one of the masses and this is in the top 10 for the challenge in my books.  Well done, and I hope you get many more voters like me... would be nice to see this on the first page for the challenge.', '2009-10-04 19:34:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674695, 824249, 32011, '<td valign="top">This a GREAT capture, and one of my top 10 images for the FS.  Love the B&amp;W processing, and the DOF here... wonderful.  But most of all, I love the story in this image.</td>', 'This a GREAT capture, and one of my top 10 images for the FS.  Love the B&W processing, and the DOF here... wonderful.  But most of all, I love the story in this image.', '2009-10-04 19:35:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674696, 824813, 32011, '<td valign="top">This is just TOO sweet.  I love the genuineness of this... yes, it''s soft, and noisy, though, your B&amp;W process has gone a long way to counter that... but I just love this image SO much... this is a beautiful image that these two will love when they grow up.  Wonderful.</td>', 'This is just TOO sweet.  I love the genuineness of this... yes, it''s soft, and noisy, though, your B&W process has gone a long way to counter that... but I just love this image SO much... this is a beautiful image that these two will love when they grow up.  Wonderful.', '2009-10-04 19:35:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5674698, 824557, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Very interesting from a technical and artistic perspective. Is this a Lensbaby shot?? So rare to see them in colour and it works really well. So many good parts to this image, the detailed, contrasty bricks, the golden light through the arch - such a range it almost loos HDR. The really interesting thing about this image is its ambiguity as to the time of day - after all that could be the sun or the moon - I suspect the moon because of the darkness on the far right of the image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: You know that I''m going to moan about the verticals... I just don''t think you can have verticals this close to it without it being perfect... and it isn;t.<br/> <br/>Overall: An intriguing picture which brings something a little different.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Very interesting from a technical and artistic perspective. Is this a Lensbaby shot?? So rare to see them in colour and it works really well. So many good parts to this image, the detailed, contrasty bricks, the golden light through the arch - such a range it almost loos HDR. The really interesting thing about this image is its ambiguity as to the time of day - after all that could be the sun or the moon - I suspect the moon because of the darkness on the far right of the image. Critical stuff: You know that I''m going to moan about the verticals... I just don''t think you can have verticals this close to it without it being perfect... and it isn;t. Overall: An intriguing picture which brings something a little different.', '2009-10-04 19:36:32.000000', NULL, 1),
