(5680903, 824961, 76335, '<td valign="top">I should have known (but honest, I didn''t!). Can''t believe this didn''t do better. Oh wait -- it''s not a landscape or an owl or Iceland. Yes I can. <br/> <br/>Regarding the more DOF comment, I respectfully disagree. There''s enough there to convey the message; anything more would have overpowered the young subject in all his wonder and innocence. <br/> <br/>Great job!</td>', 'I should have known (but honest, I didn''t!). Can''t believe this didn''t do better. Oh wait -- it''s not a landscape or an owl or Iceland. Yes I can.  Regarding the more DOF comment, I respectfully disagree. There''s enough there to convey the message; anything more would have overpowered the young subject in all his wonder and innocence.  Great job!', '2009-10-08 19:38:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5680910, 823720, 82707, '<td valign="top">Nice image! I like the colours and you''ve done a great job on the lighting.</td>', 'Nice image! I like the colours and you''ve done a great job on the lighting.', '2009-10-08 19:43:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5680911, 822180, 68504, '<td valign="top">This one is stunning.</td>', 'This one is stunning.', '2009-10-08 19:44:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5680913, 821510, 41299, '<td valign="top">Thanks bvy ;)<br/> <br/>You are totally correct. The whole design was thought through thouroughly, and this was the best way I could get the image across. There''s always someone to criticize an image - beauty is in the eye of the beholder and every individual has it''s own unique taste. Some (or many) on DPC have their personal tastes flavoured by rules of thumb like these rules are the law. Photography rules of thumb are mere guidelines if you ask me. They are to be interpreted by the person composing and taking the picture and they should be applied or at least be kept in mind but only there where they contribute to the overall composition and layout of a photo.<br/>In this particular image I decided to ignore the rules and go for my best feeling; hoping to get that feeling across. You, and a few others have picked up on the message ;)</td>', 'Thanks bvy ;) You are totally correct. The whole design was thought through thouroughly, and this was the best way I could get the image across. There''s always someone to criticize an image - beauty is in the eye of the beholder and every individual has it''s own unique taste. Some (or many) on DPC have their personal tastes flavoured by rules of thumb like these rules are the law. Photography rules of thumb are mere guidelines if you ask me. They are to be interpreted by the person composing and taking the picture and they should be applied or at least be kept in mind but only there where they contribute to the overall composition and layout of a photo.In this particular image I decided to ignore the rules and go for my best feeling; hoping to get that feeling across. You, and a few others have picked up on the message ;)', '2009-10-08 19:50:00.000000', NULL, 0),
