(5681192, 824924, 108687, '<td valign="top">Aeroguri, thanks for the comments. I will try it on the image as practice. I really liked the way 8th place looked also. <br/> <br/>mpeters, the catchlights were produced by a 580 EXII shot into a 32" silver umbrella at camera left.  This was my first shoot using that set-up.</td>', 'Aeroguri, thanks for the comments. I will try it on the image as practice. I really liked the way 8th place looked also.  mpeters, the catchlights were produced by a 580 EXII shot into a 32" silver umbrella at camera left.  This was my first shoot using that set-up.', '2009-10-08 22:55:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5681223, 824948, 24486, '<td valign="top">That''s funny, we both did birds this month. I was fairly sure this was yours. My first thought when I saw it in voting was the same as <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=63398" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">NikonJeb</a> that it looked like a plate in a bird book. Really nice work Rina.</td>', 'That''s funny, we both did birds this month. I was fairly sure this was yours. My first thought when I saw it in voting was the same as  NikonJeb that it looked like a plate in a bird book. Really nice work Rina.', '2009-10-08 23:11:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5681245, 823134, 53814, '<td valign="top">The photo really is wonderful. Mesmerizing motion and contrasting elements... I see Neptune, morphing into an angry sea-bird, about to devour the graffiti-like reflection. <br/> <br/>You, especially, could pen a treatise debating the wisdom of entering photographic art into a contest designed to judge stock photography. This photo probably belongs in an art gallery. I don''t understand why you, even briefly, considered the possibility it would be received/scored well at DPC. <br/> <br/></td>', 'The photo really is wonderful. Mesmerizing motion and contrasting elements... I see Neptune, morphing into an angry sea-bird, about to devour the graffiti-like reflection.  You, especially, could pen a treatise debating the wisdom of entering photographic art into a contest designed to judge stock photography. This photo probably belongs in an art gallery. I don''t understand why you, even briefly, considered the possibility it would be received/scored well at DPC.  ', '2009-10-08 23:31:15.000000', NULL, 0),
