(5694376, 824948, 47541, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. I''ve been stalking Tui''s in the trees off my deck for ages now but I''ve not yet managed to get a shot that I''m happy with, after all, you''ve got to be able to show their fantastic colours off. This shot manages to do this. <br/> <br/>On the negative side, the feathers seem just a little soft, maybe it''s the DOF or the shutter speed (neither of which you list). I''d also have cloned out that OOF branch in the front as it seems to interupt the nice line of the branch he (or she) is sitting on.<br/> <br/>Looking at this more I see one of the problems I have with my Tui stalking. The main tree we have for them is a Kowhai and it seems to have many more branches than your tree, hence less "clean" shots of the Tui''s. I''m not giving up though, even if I have to grab a chainsaw to "tidy" the tree a tad!<br/> <br/>PS: I did have to laugh at <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=63398" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">NikonJeb</a>''s comment, he''s must be a real nerd if he reads "nird books" ;)</td>', 'Nice shot. I''ve been stalking Tui''s in the trees off my deck for ages now but I''ve not yet managed to get a shot that I''m happy with, after all, you''ve got to be able to show their fantastic colours off. This shot manages to do this.  On the negative side, the feathers seem just a little soft, maybe it''s the DOF or the shutter speed (neither of which you list). I''d also have cloned out that OOF branch in the front as it seems to interupt the nice line of the branch he (or she) is sitting on. Looking at this more I see one of the problems I have with my Tui stalking. The main tree we have for them is a Kowhai and it seems to have many more branches than your tree, hence less "clean" shots of the Tui''s. I''m not giving up though, even if I have to grab a chainsaw to "tidy" the tree a tad! PS: I did have to laugh at  NikonJeb''s comment, he''s must be a real nerd if he reads "nird books" ;)', '2009-10-21 02:14:28.000000', NULL, 0),
