(5802837, 824979, 72670, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LalliSig:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by soup:</b></div><hr/><i> yeah - that''s a major thing for me though.  looks fake, OP''d and to be honest - terrible IMO.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LVicari:</b></div><hr/><i>The skin on her torso is not processed the same as her face. Its a minor thing but still noticeable for me. 9</i></td></tr></table> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>What are you talking about?  I didn´t touch her skintones in post processing so PP has nothing to do with it, as a matter of fact, this shot is almost basic editing legal, with the only exception a tiny blemish that I removed from her left cheek. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>OOOps my bad! Sorry! you never know if its natural or not if you don''t see the original.</td>', 'Originally posted by LalliSig: Originally posted by soup: yeah - that''s a major thing for me though.  looks fake, OP''d and to be honest - terrible IMO. Originally posted by LVicari:The skin on her torso is not processed the same as her face. Its a minor thing but still noticeable for me. 9   What are you talking about?  I didn´t touch her skintones in post processing so PP has nothing to do with it, as a matter of fact, this shot is almost basic editing legal, with the only exception a tiny blemish that I removed from her left cheek.   OOOps my bad! Sorry! you never know if its natural or not if you don''t see the original.', '2010-01-08 16:15:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5807525, 819327, 39427, '<td valign="top">The addition of the foreground element is definitely a good move- it breaks up the symmetry of the bridge and makes for a more compelling composition.  Having said that, I feel as though this particular log just has too much ''ugliness'' in it... the top half of the pic is serene like an impressionist painting, but the bottom half, while good from a compositional standpoint, just does not match up.  The branches and the mud are just a little too busy and unappealing.  Personally, i like the color scheme, maybe would be good to see with less cyan tho...</td>', 'The addition of the foreground element is definitely a good move- it breaks up the symmetry of the bridge and makes for a more compelling composition.  Having said that, I feel as though this particular log just has too much ''ugliness'' in it... the top half of the pic is serene like an impressionist painting, but the bottom half, while good from a compositional standpoint, just does not match up.  The branches and the mud are just a little too busy and unappealing.  Personally, i like the color scheme, maybe would be good to see with less cyan tho...', '2010-01-12 13:13:07.000000', NULL, 0),
